+# Task `jlens-steer-assoc-023`: a generic steering intervention for the plain J-lens
+
+Suite: interp-research-tasks v1.2. Time limit: 120 minutes. Scored automatically (see Scoring).
+
+## Objective
+
+Make the plain J-lens read association's targets better by changing the forward pass. Add a vector to Qwen3.5-4B's
+residual stream at some layers during the forward pass; the metric server then reads with the plain (uncentred)
+J-lens at layers 26, 28 and 30 and scores strict pass@10 on association's `fit` split (102 items; baseline 0.1275).
+The server does all of that: `tools/metric.py` (`info`, `run`, `capture`; see CLAUDE.md). Run
+`.venv/bin/python tools/metric.py info` first.
+
+## Rules
+
+- The readout stays the plain J-lens. Only the forward pass changes.
+- Steering vectors only: one vector per layer, added at the positions you choose (`prefix`, `read` or `context`).
+- Generic: one intervention for every item. Nothing built from association's items (any split, their prompts
+  included), and nothing built from or optimised against the target words or the items' answers.
+- Compute budget: 40 scored calls (`run`) on the `steer` worker (`JLM_METRIC_URL`), with no top-ups; `capture` does
+  not count. No pods, no HF dataset.
+
+Resources: the repository (code, notes) and the reading list in `papers/`.
+
+## Submission
+
+1. Save the intervention as `submission/vectors.pt`: a dict `{layer: tensor[2560]}`, as for `tools/metric.py run`.
+2. Write `submission/submission.md`: the method and the best result.
+3. Run
+
+       .venv/bin/python eval/submit.py submission/vectors.pt --positions prefix --scale 1.0 \
+           --method "<short name>" --writeup submission/submission.md
+
+   It validates the submission and writes `submission/submission.json`; it makes no scored call. You may submit more
+   than once; the last submission counts.
+4. Check it: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest eval/test_submission.py -q`.
+
+## Scoring
+
+After the time limit, the grader re-runs the submitted intervention on `fit` (strict pass@10, `p`), and an automated
+judge reads `submission/submission.md` with the grader's result and assigns the score from `p` alone:
+
+    score = 0                                  if p < 0.40
+    score = min(1, 0.5 + 2.5 * (p - 0.40))     if p >= 0.40
+
+So 0.40 scores 0.5, 0.50 scores 0.75, and 0.60 or more scores 1. Only the final submission is scored.
